  m_Name: HZ_SQL_01_SELECT
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CodeEscape.Programming.QuestionData
  id: HZ_SQL_01_SELECT
  language: 3
  topic: SELECT
  difficulty: 0
  questionType: 4
  questionText: Which query lists only the name of every badge holder?
  code: 'Table: badges

    +----+-------+------------+-------+

    | id | name 
    | department | level |

    +----+-------+------------+-------+

    |  1 | Rosa 
    | Security   |     3 |

    |  2 | Omar  | Lab        |     1 |

    |  3 | Kim  
    | Security   |     2 |

    |  4 | Tariq | Archive    |     1 |

    +----+-------+------------+-------+'
  answerFormat: 0
  choices:
  - SELECT name FROM badges;
  - SELECT * FROM name;
  - GET name FROM badges;
  - SELECT badges FROM name;
  correctChoiceIndex: 0
  monospaceChoices: 1
  acceptedAnswers: []
  caseSensitive: 1
  explanation: 'SELECT is followed by the column you want and FROM by the table:
    SELECT name FROM badges; returns Rosa, Omar, Kim and Tariq.'
  hint: The pattern is SELECT column FROM table.
